."], "quotes": [{"text": "Nothing to it but clearing out underbrush and limbs so teams can get to the logs. […] If anyone asks, just tell him you've swamped roads ever since you was big enough to lift a hatchet.", "reference": "1954, W. E. Blackhurst, Riders of the Flood, page 27:"}, {"text": "\"Hayburners,\" or horses, their \"teamsters,\" and oxen driven by their \"bullwhackers,\" all became outmoded, as did \"crosspoling\" logs across trails to make them sturdy and \"swamping,\" or cutting, new trails to \"snake\" logs out of the forest.", "reference": "2006, Harold Farwell, Logging Terminology, page 1021:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}